formal_description.statement:
The arrival curve eta_delta_t describes the maximum number of events which can arrive during any given time window delta_t. The minimum distance between n subsequent events delta_n is its pseudo-inverse.

delta_n = min_delta_t_ge_0_delta_t_in_R {delta_t | eta_delta_t >= n}
eta_delta_t = max_n_ge_1_n_in_N {n | delta_n <= delta_t}

For a bursty input with period P, jitter J, and minimal distance d_min:
delta_n = max((n - 1) * d_min, (n - 1) * P - J)

